## Node reports: treeview.py and chessai-treeview (2026-11-11)

`leagues/treeview.py MODEL` writes a node-by-node HTML report of a tree or DAG (usage in its docstring; MODEL is
`EXPERIMENT:LINE@V`, a global `LINE@V`, or `bdt:`/`bdd:PATH`). It generalises models/from-scratch/leafview.
- Exact numbers come from `models/from-scratch/bin/chessai-treeview`, a new binary (no league uses it), built from
  `models/from-scratch/fastbin/treeview-src` (chessai-errdag3's source plus three commands; `nice -n 15 cargo build
  --release -j 2`, installed by copy and rename):
  - `node-dump MODEL OUT GAMES... [--use-probs] [--leaf-odds] [--routes-stdout]`: `OUT/model.json` (every node:
    kind, children, classifier text, counters, window means, sibling sets, path tables) and `OUT/games.tsv`; per
    position its game, ply, result, features, router hops with their scores, leaf, probabilities and (with
    --leaf-odds) every leaf's log-odds, to `OUT/routes.tsv` or, with --routes-stdout, to stdout (treeview.py streams
    it; nothing per position is kept). Checked against `eval-loss`: same leaves, same log-loss.
  - `node-history OUT MODEL...`: one JSON line per model, without classifier texts (window history, node dating).
  - `path-stats` now also reads round directories of game directories (identical output on merged copies).
- The cache, `models/from-scratch/treeview-cache/`: `games/` (hard-linked snapshots of the leagues' rounds, reused for
  two hours), `slots/` (per model directory: model.json, games.tsv, the dump's stderr; rewritten each run), `hist/`
  (one small JSON per model version read), `pages/` (the dashboard's reports). `dumps/` (2.6 GB) and `parts/`
  (168 MB) are from the first version and unused: safe to delete.
- Window standard errors are not in model files. For a DAG's routers the report estimates how close a window came to
  a router split from the line's latest `.state` (the SE of each router's last window, taken for all its windows),
  as models/from-scratch/errdag/trigger/closeness.py does; it agrees with it (z=160 #1 of error-dag-p1: t 157.0).
- Runtime: 4-10 s per model on ~200k positions, about 1.3 cores (the model's and the flat model's dumps stream
